"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{64}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{49}=1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-6)^{2}}{{8}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{7}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=3$ and $k=6.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,6\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7a88a33c96022b001d503335496ca3ca20930aba3db57ba745ae5290035086" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y=12?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y & =12 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-12y-3{x}^{2}+12x & =12 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}-6y]-3[{x}^{2}-4x] & =12 \\\\ 2[(y-3)^{2}-9]-3[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-18-3(x-2)^{2}+12 & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =12+18-12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999f72ca01cb996b0139ea810637ab9c20e94bd9af51ba2022fb" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6d7a88a33c96022b001d503335496ca3ca20930aba3db57ba745ae5290035086" "basis" 580 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13949542/state.json" "file_sha256" "04180657b303999