r/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328296" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x+7)^{2}}{6}=1?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{5}-\\frac{(x-(-7))^{2}}{6}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h=-7$ and $k=0.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(-7,0).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-6,5)"] ["math" "(-7,0)"] ["math" "(0,-7)"] ["math" "(5,6)"] ["math" "(7,0)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78869" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(-7,0)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y=7$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+2y & =7 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-2y) & =7 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-1)^{2}+1 & =7 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =7+4-1 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-1)^{2} & =10 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{5/2}-\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,1\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328358" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-274638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}-54x+64y=-1$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-274638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2}-54x+64y & =-1 \\\\ 9{x}^{2}-54x-16{y}^{2}+64y & =-1 \\\\ 9[{x}^{2}-6x]-16[{y}^{2}-4y] & =-1 \\\\ 9[(x-3)^{2}-9]-16[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-81-16(y-2)^{2}+64 & =-1 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-16(y-2)^{2} & =-1+81-64 \\\\ 9(x-3)^{2}-16(y-2)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{(\\frac{4}{3})}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,3,2\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-274638" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-274638" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "ca