es:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-24x+10y & =7 \\\\ 6({x}^{2}-4x)-({y}^{2}-10y) & =7 \\\\ 6[(x-2)^{2}-4]-[(y-5)^{2}-25] & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-24-(y-5)^{2}+25 & =7 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =7+24-25 \\\\ 6(x-2)^{2}-(y-5)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{1}-\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{6}=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,2,5\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328374" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-328374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328374" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328374" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328374" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y=11$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, group the $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}-8x+6y & =11 \\\\ 4({x}^{2}-2x)-({y}^{2}-6y) & =11 \\\\ 4[(x-1)^{2}-1]-[(y-3)^{2}-9] & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-4-(y-3)^{2}+9 & =11 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =11+4-9 \\\\ 4(x-1)^{2}-(y-3)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{3/2}-\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,3\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328355" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y=-13?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2{y}^{2}-18x+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-18x-2{y}^{2}+8y & =-13 \\\\ 3[{x}^{2}-6x]-2[{y}^{2}-4y] & =-13 \\\\ 3[(x-3)^{2}-9]-2[(y-2)^{2}-4] & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-27-2(y-2)^{2}+8 & =-13 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =-13+27-8 \\\\ 3(x-3)^{2}-2(y-2)^{2} & =6 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(3,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-1)"] ["math" "(-3,-2)"] ["math" "(1,-3)"] ["math" "(2,-3)"] ["math" "(3,2)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(3,2)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y=-108$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{y}^{2}-16{x}^{2}-72y & =-108 \\\\ 9{y}^{2}-72y-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9[{y}^{2}-8y]-16[{x}^{2}] & =-108 \\\\ 9[(y-4)^{2}-16]-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-144-16{x}^{2} & =-108 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =-108+144 \\\\ 9(y-4)^{2}-16{x}^{2} & =36 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9/4} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,0,4\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328403" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The center of the hyperbola $-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16$ is$\\,\\,($\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-16{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-8y+32x=16 \\\\ {y}^{2}-8y\\,-\\,16{x}^{2}+32x & =16 \\\\ [{y}^{2}-8y]\\,-\\,16[{x}^{2}-2x] & =16 \\\\ [(y-4)^{2}-16]\\,-\\,16\\,[(x-1)^{2}-1] & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16\\,-\\,16(x-1)^{2}+16 & =16 \\\\ (y-4)^{2}-16(x-1)^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{1} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{{1}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center of the hyperbola is $(\\,1,4\\,).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-328400" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12x+24y=-9?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{x}^{2}+3{y}^{2}+12x+24y & =-9 \\\\ 3{y}^{2}+24y-{x}^{2}+12x & =-9 \\\\ 3[{y}^{2}+8y]-[{x}^{2}-12x] & =-9 \\\\ 3[(y+4)^{2}-16]-[(x-6)^{2}-36] & =-9 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-48-(x-6)^{2}+36 & =-9 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-(x-6)^{2} & =-9+48-36 \\\\ 3(y+4)^{2}-(x-6)^{2} & =3 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-6)^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(6,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-4,6)"] ["math" "(-6,4)"] ["math" "(1,3)"] ["math" "(3,-1)"] ["math" "(6,-4)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116118" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(6,-4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y=12?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+2{y}^{2}+12x-12y & =12 \\\\ 2{y}^{2}-12y-3{x}^{2}+12x & =12 \\\\ 2[{y}^{2}-6y]-3[{x}^{2}-4x] & =12 \\\\ 2[(y-3)^{2}-9]-3[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-18-3(x-2)^{2}+12 & =12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =12+18-12 \\\\ 2(y-3)^{2}-3(x-2)^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,3).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "(-2,-3)"] ["math" "(-3,-2)"] ["math" "(2,3)"] ["math" "(3,6)"] ["math" "(6,9)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-78379" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(2,3)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$-3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-24x+8y=41?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-24x+8y & =41 \\\\ {y}^{2}+8y-3{x}^{2}-24x & =41 \\\\ [{y}^{2}+8y]-3[{x}^{2}+8x] & =41 \\\\ [(y+4)^{2}-16]-3[(x+4)^{2}-16] & =41 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-16-3(x+4)^{2}+48 & =41 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-3(x+4)^{2} & =41+16-48 \\\\ (y+4)^{2}-3(x+4)^{2} & =9 \\\\ \\frac{(y+4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{3} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-(-4))^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-(-4))^{2}}{(\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-4,-4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/state.json" "file_sha256" "d00bf355d986c08d1593e7a8a7ea50e8eb2e69c11b0d365075b02f3110f294db"} {"question" "q-116122" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14037937/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b57cc720ea4d8670a02a0f1544efdb115af4403f3e5c6b7146f8a0fb739dfe70"} {"question" "q-116122"